; THE QUAY - a place that is not a fight, which is the whole point of it.
;
; Saltmarch is the THIRD campaign test (PLACES_AND_PERSISTENCE.md, the World layer). ashfall and
; greyhollow proved a dungeon is data; this proves a WORLD is - somewhere to stand, people to deal
; with, a way out, a road with something on it, and a quest that can be failed - and like both of
; them it was authored with a text editor and no new C# was written to make it exist.
;
; Nobody hostile is drawn on this map. The spawn slots are people and things: Norrel on 1, the
; lockbox on 2, his grave on 3 (which is empty ground until it isn't), and the marsh road out on 4.
; The same numbers, doing something that is not a fight, is the reframe in one file.
;
;   .  floor      ~  difficult ground   #  rock      @  the hero starts
;   1-9 a spawn   |  wall up a line     -  wall along a line   x  door, shut   +  a corner

